  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis is the first slice of #3919. The built-in holder library gets seven more tapers. Each taper has ER collet chucks and Weldon side-lock holders. The outlines use the existing conservative laws of `holder_library.rs`: a full flange cylinder, a 45-degree flare envelope, and a profile that stops at the gauge line.\n\n- `crates/tools/src/holder_library_din.rs`: SK30 and SK40 (DIN 69871 / DIN ISO 7388-1), and ISO30, the router name for the same size 30 taper and flange.\n- `crates/tools/src/holder_library_hsk.rs`: HSK-A63, HSK-F63, HSK-E40, HSK-E32 (DIN 69893-1 / -5 / -6). The plane face is the gauge line. The collar (f1) is drawn as a full cylinder at d1.\n- `crates/tools/src/holder_library.rs`: a `family()` helper builds the entries of one taper. The file has 391 lines.\n- `docs/decisions/3919-standard-holders.md`: each number and its source, the entry list, and what this slice leaves out.\n\nNumbers (mm):\n\n| Taper | Flange Ø | Standoff | Flange / collar | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SK30, ISO30 | 50 | 3.2 | 15.9 | Haimer DIN ISO 7388-1 table; \"SK40_DIN69871.pdf\" data sheet; Techniks router catalog (ISO30 Ø50) |\n| SK40 | 63.55 | 3.2 | 15.9 | the same two tables |\n| HSK-A63 | 63 | 0 | 26 | ISCAR 1352.pdf; GDP Tooling; Haimer |\n| HSK-F63 | 63 | 0 | 26 | GDP Tooling; Haimer; TAC Rockford |\n| HSK-E40 | 40 | 0 | 20 | GDP Tooling; TAC Rockford |\n| HSK-E32 | 32 | 0 | 20 | GDP Tooling; TAC Rockford |\n\nThe taper names have no space (`HSK-A63`). Reason: the grouped Weldon pick (#2018) reads a two-word name.\n\nNot in this slice (the decision file has the reasons):\n- ISO20 and ISO25: no table gives the gauge Ø, the distance from the gauge line to the flange, or the flange thickness.\n- R8: no standard describes the steel below the spindle nose. The existing \"ER.. chuck\" entries give the same shape.\n- SF32: the shoulder below the taper and the datum of the catalog L are missing. The issue comment lists them.\n- Machine files: `tooling.spindle_mount` does not accept the new tapers yet. Follow-up #4239.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `holder_library::din::tests::the_din_69871_tapers_match_the_recorded_table`\n- `holder_library::din::tests::the_din_entries_are_listed`\n- `holder_library::din::tests::the_sk40_er32_outline_is_the_table`\n- `holder_library::din::tests::an_iso30_holder_draws_its_sk30_twin`\n- `holder_library::hsk::tests::the_hsk_tapers_match_the_recorded_table`\n- `holder_library::hsk::tests::the_hsk_entries_are_listed`\n- `holder_library::hsk::tests::the_hsk_a63_er32_outline_is_the_table`\n- `holder_library::hsk::tests::a_nose_wider_than_the_collar_steps_in_to_it`\n- `holder_library::hsk::tests::every_hsk_profile_tops_out_at_the_plane_face`\n- Updated: `holder_library::weldon::tests::the_picker_shows_one_weldon_row_for_each_taper` (it lists the 11 tapers).\n- The existing laws run over every new entry: `every_entry_draws_a_valid_profile_with_its_flange_and_nose` and `the_flare_envelope_runs_45_degrees_into_the_flange_front` (tools), and `every_entry_reads_the_same_bands_by_reference_as_its_old_copy` (app `holder_reference`).\n\n## Gate (winbuild, Windows, head `62516f35e`)\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 2 steps (tools lib, app `mcp_holder`), 0 failed, 0 stalled.\n- Strict clippy `-p camcraft-tools --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean (exit 0).\n- app `holder_reference`: 12 passed. app `holder_library`: 7 passed.\n- ui lib tests filtered on `tool_holder` and `tool_library_holders`: 12 passed.\n- The light lane was not run. Its twins are motion and app toolpath tests, and this diff does not reach them. No heavy step (P6).\n\nLight lane: not run. Its twins are motion and app toolpath tests, and this diff (the tools holder library only) does not reach them. No heavy step (P6).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- I did not open the GUI. The tool library window lists the new rows through `holder_library::library()`. The ui tests `tool_holder` and `tool_library_holders` ran in the gate.\n- I did not post-process a program with a new holder. A holder outline changes the collision checks only, not the posted G-code.\n\nChangelog: The holder library adds HSK-A63, HSK-F63, HSK-E40, HSK-E32, SK30, SK40 and router ISO30 holders, each with ER collet chucks and Weldon side-lock holders.\n\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nRefs #3919\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
